@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+dobe-write: private headless document engine
+
+Commands: convert, info, text, inspect, snapshot, picture, glyphs, render, run, commands, parity.
+Editable formats include DOCX and the full native JSON document model.
+PDF and PNG exports support --strict to refuse missing glyphs or pictures.
+Default paper uses en-GB/A4; explicit document page settings remain authoritative.
+Font discovery uses the pinned embedded fonts, never ambient system font directories.
+No editor bridge, standalone MCP, Zotero connection or automatic language-pack store.
+Use the Dobe CLI or product MCP for durable customer operations when qualified.
+This private component is not an untrusted-document sandbox or a release-qualified application.
+snapshot FILE emits every serialized native document field without saving or laying it out.
+The snapshot also reports missing pictures and retained-markup presence; JSON does not preserve that read-time state. Retain the source document.
+Cached DATE/TIME fields change only after an explicit field update. Proofing and hyphenation are not qualified.
+picture FILE fully decodes one bounded raster without opening a document or loading fonts.
+Its stdout is DOBEPIC1, a little-endian u32 JSON-header length, that JSON header, then exact RGBA8 pixels.
+This diagnostic packet is private; resource admission still requires an independent decoder comparison.
+glyphs FILE traces actual PNG-display glyph IDs, text ranges, geometry and exact font bytes.
+Its stdout is DOBEGLY1, a little-endian u32 JSON-header length, that header, then owned font bytes.
+This opens and lays out the document: prior admission is mandatory. Watermarks and outline-only text are refused.
+Glyph traces are diagnostics, not independent shaping proof or permission to embed a font.
